{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.217,
   "text": "I close the town library on Friday nights, and the head librarian gave me one rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.817,
   "end": 16.409,
   "text": "If a book comes through the return slot after nine... don't check it in. Leave it in the bin until morning."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 17.209,
   "end": 19.769,
   "text": "For two months, nothing came."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.869,
   "end": 25.925,
   "text": "Then last Friday, at nine fourteen, I heard the metal slot creak open."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 28.325,
   "end": 29.055,
   "text": "Thump."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 30.455,
   "end": 37.239,
   "text": "A small black book. No title. No barcode. Just an old paper checkout card, tucked inside the cover."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 37.939,
   "end": 43.869,
   "text": "The names on the card were night clerks. I knew them from the faded photos in the break room."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 44.569,
   "end": 50.009,
   "text": "Next to each name, a date in red ink... the day each one stopped showing up for work."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 50.809,
   "end": 53.775,
   "text": "The last line was empty. Waiting."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 55.375,
   "end": 60.431,
   "text": "I didn't touch it. I turned off the lights, locked the doors, and walked to my car."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 61.031,
   "end": 65.425,
   "text": "Behind me, the return slot creaked open... and stayed open."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 67.425,
   "end": 70.967,
   "text": "When I got home, there was something in my coat pocket."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 72.167,
   "end": 78.204,
   "text": "The checkout card. My name was on the last line... and the red stamp beside it said: Due tonight."
  }
 ],
